@{ ViewData["Title"] = "About"; }
<section class="panel">
    <div class="panel-head">About myPTO</div>
    <div class="panel-body">
        <p>A Permission To Occupy (PTO) is the official document that lets a household live on a municipal site
           while the formal title process is completed. myPTO lets Mangaung residents apply online, upload their
           documents, track the application and request a renewal.</p>
        <p>A PTO is valid for @WebConstants.PtoValidityMonths months. We send a reminder @WebConstants.ExpiryWarningDays days
           before it expires so you can renew in time.</p>
        <div class="section-title">How is the decision made?</div>
        <p>Sites are limited in every area. Nobody at the municipality approves applications by hand: the system verifies your documents
           and, when the area has received enough applications, it ranks the applicants and gives the free sites to the most needy and most
           qualifying. Lower income, being a military veteran, being elderly and having dependants all raise your score. If your score is
           too low or the sites are full you are rejected and can apply for another area. You renew or de-register your own PTO.</p>
        <div class="section-title">Who can apply?</div>
        <ul>
            <li>Household income below R@(WebConstants.MaxMonthlyIncome.ToString("N0")) per month</li>
            <li>South African citizen</li>
            <li>First-time home owner and first-time subsidy recipient</li>
            <li>Over 21 years old</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="panel-foot"><a class="btn" asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index">Back</a></div>
</section>
